Role/Tools.pm:359-368 response_tool_calls (hermes) splits the RAW hermes_extract_content text, thinking included. chat_f (Role/Chat.pm ~l.951) lifts from Response->content, which chat_response already think-filtered, and _hermes_stream_split (Tools.pm:264ff, k302) deliberately treats a call inside <think> as no call. So chat_with_tools_f (and Chat simple_chat_with_tools[_f]) runs tools the model only considered in its reasoning.

Repro: NousResearch (think_tag_filter=1), content "<think>I could call <tool_call>{\"name\":\"echo\",\"arguments\":{\"m\":\"x\"}}</tool_call> but no need.</think>The answer is 4." -> loop executes echo once; chat_f with the same tools gives content "The answer is 4.", tool_calls 0.

Fix: when think_tag_filter is on, strip thinking (filter_think_content, orphan </think> rule of k302) before _hermes_split_text in response_tool_calls; keep the raw content for the assistant echo in format_tool_results. Test in t/43_hermes_stream_tool_calls.t sibling / t/6x.
